      <p><strong>Harold Dean Smoked Goods</strong> is the BBQ spot in Flower Mound that locals keep quietly to themselves — which is their own fault for not spreading the word sooner. Named after "Paw Paw," a family patriarch whose weekends revolved around feeding people, this smokehouse carries genuine soul. Meats are smoked over native pecan wood at a precise 210°F, which creates a slightly sweet, clean smoke flavor that's distinctly different from the post-oak-only approach you'll find elsewhere. The brisket has excellent bark and doesn't need sauce (though the house sauce — a family recipe — is also excellent). The black pepper sausage is a must-order. On Thursday, Friday, and Saturday nights, they also offer steaks. Thursday nights bring live music, turning dinner into an event. If you haven't been, go.</p>

